where $n$ is the number of edges of the tensor, and $S_t$ is a third-order function, see App.~\ref{app:ithorder}.

The tensor-network representation of third-order circuits can be obtained directly from the circuit description.
First, each CSS gate can be replaced by a small tensor-network composed of $X$ and $Z$ tensors~\cite{kissinger2022phasefree}, when post-selected onto the $+1$ outcome.
Each $n$-qubit third-level diagonal gate is represented by a single third-order tensor with $n$ open edges.
This tensor is connected to the qubit worldlines, in between the CSS gates on which it acts, via a $Z$ tensor.
