$M^b$ is symmetric by Cor.~\ref{cor:derivates-symmetric}, as it is defined by a derivative.

To show that $M^b$ is independent of the chosen $A$, we consider the difference of matrix elements obtained from two different $A\neq A'$, with the same coboundary $d_1A = b$, using tri-linearity of $\Delta^{(3)}S$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
    (\Delta^{(3)}S)(A,d_0v, d_0w) - (\Delta^{(3)}S)(A',d_0v, d_0w)\\
